<article class="env-lemma" id="0877">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0877">Lemma <span data-tag="0877">76.37.2</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $f : X \to Y$ be a morphism of algebraic spaces over $S$. Let $V \subset Y$ be an open subspace. Assume </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$f$ is locally of finite type and flat, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$V \to Y$ is quasi-compact and scheme theoretically dense, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$f|_{f^{-1}V} : f^{-1}V \to V$ is locally of finite presentation. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
  <p> Then $f$ is of locally of finite presentation. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      The proof is identical to the proof of Lemma <a href="/tag/0876" data-tag="0876">76.37.1</a> except one uses More on Flatness, Lemma <a href="/tag/081P" data-tag="081P">38.11.2</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>